BC-250 / Cyan Skillfish: widen SMU SCLK range to 350–2230 MHz

AMD ships cyan skillfish with SCLK_MIN=1000 and SCLK_MAX=2000, well
inside the hardware's actual 350–2230 MHz envelope. This widens the
constants so userspace SMU-based governors (e.g. cyan-skillfish-governor)
can drive the full clock range. Does not change default behavior — only
expands the validated limits.

From MastaG/linux-cachyos-bc250 kernel-7.1 patch set.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/cyan_skillfish_ppt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/cyan_skillfish_ppt.c
@@ -45,8 +45,8 @@
 #undef pr_debug
 
 /* unit: MHz */
-#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN			1000
-#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MAX			2000
+#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN			350
+#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MAX			2230
 
 /* unit: mV */
 #define CYAN_SKILLFISH_VDDC_MIN			700
